
==============================================================================
A. The isometry fact and the growth under a rotation applied per Link
==============================================================================
n_s = C'[s]^2 + S'[s]^2 over the 2N = 128 settings: min 65242, max 65824 (65536 exact only where an entry is 0 or 256)
a rotation at s = 21 applied once per Link: the amplitude norm x n_s = 65824 and the multiplicity x 65536 per Link;
   L =  1: multiplicity 65536^L = 2^16, within 2^62; norm factor n_s^L = 6.582e+04
   L =  2: multiplicity 65536^L = 2^32, within 2^62; norm factor n_s^L = 4.333e+09
   L =  3: multiplicity 65536^L = 2^48, within 2^62; norm factor n_s^L = 2.852e+14
   L =  4: multiplicity 65536^L = 2^64, BEYOND 2^62; norm factor n_s^L = 1.877e+19
   L =  8: multiplicity 65536^L = 2^128, BEYOND 2^62; norm factor n_s^L = 3.524e+38
   L = 64: multiplicity 2^1024: BEYOND 2^62 by 2^962
so a per-Link application of the tables overflows the register's ceiling at the fourth Link of any path.

==============================================================================
B. The angle-index form: two labels, one rate per Link, the tables once at the click
==============================================================================
a row born on label 0 (amplitude 1), the record's label angle sigma advanced by s per Link mod 2N,
the click at an analyser of setting a applies U_(sigma + a) once: channel + weight C'^2, channel - weight S'^2;
the counts over the 64 births by the ladder, at three distances, for s = 3 per Link and a = 0:
   L sigma     C2     S2      w+      w-  counts +/-  cos^2 (report)
   0     0    256      0   65536       0     [64, 0]          1.0000
   5    15    190    172   36100   29584    [35, 29]          0.5490
  10    30     25    255     625   65025     [1, 63]          0.0096
  16    48   -181    181   32761   32761    [32, 32]          0.5000
  21    63   -256     13   65536     169     [64, 0]          0.9976
  32    96      0   -256       0   65536     [0, 64]          0.0000
  43     1    256     13   65536     169     [64, 0]          0.9976
  64    64   -256      0   65536       0     [64, 0]          1.0000
the multiplicity: the birth's norm x 65536 once (the click's table), whatever L: within the ceiling for every path length.
exactness: an angle added mod 2N is exact; the one table lookup rounds once (n_sigma / 65536 within 0.36 %), as the design's window does.

==============================================================================
C. Three labels (the neutrino's families): the mixing at the ends, a phase per Link per label
==============================================================================
U at scale 65536 (s12 = 11, s23 = 16): [[56320, 33792, 0], [-23892, 39820, 46336], [23892, -39820, 46336]]
the rows' norms (65536^2 = 4294967296 ideal): [4313841664, 4303484960, 4303484960]
the phase rates per Link per label: (0, 5, 9) steps of N = 64; born as flavour 0 (row 0 of U): the labels' amplitudes [56320, 33792, 0]
at the click the analyser reads flavour beta: a_beta = sum_j U[beta][j] x U[0][j] x (C[phi_j], S[phi_j]), phi_j = rates_j x L mod N;
the weights |a_beta|^2 (scale 65536^2 x 256 per amplitude component), the counts over 64 births by the ladder:
   L         phases                                    weights (0, 1, 2)         counts             P (report)
   0      [0, 0, 0]                    [1219574490861554165088256, 0, 0]     [64, 0, 0]        [1.0, 0.0, 0.0]
   8     [0, 40, 8] [409146810681372927066112, 405092802632695676928000, 405092802632695676928000]   [21, 22, 21]  [0.336, 0.332, 0.332]
  16    [0, 16, 16] [744826635422367855149056, 237323219177905009459200, 237323219177905009459200]   [39, 13, 12]  [0.611, 0.195, 0.195]
  24    [0, 56, 24] [1080469950013347318464512, 69502938013939374489600, 69502938013939374489600]     [57, 3, 4]  [0.886, 0.057, 0.057]
  32    [0, 32, 32] [270078779983181545209856, 474646438355810018918400, 474646438355810018918400]   [14, 25, 25]  [0.221, 0.389, 0.389]
  48    [0, 48, 48] [744826635422367855149056, 237323219177905009459200, 237323219177905009459200]   [39, 13, 12]  [0.611, 0.195, 0.195]
  64      [0, 0, 0]                    [1219574490861554165088256, 0, 0]     [64, 0, 0]        [1.0, 0.0, 0.0]
the multiplicity: the birth's row at scale 256 (norm 65536 = 2^16) and the click's rows at scale 65536 (norm 2^32): 2^48 per path, within 2^62;
   a mixing applied per Link instead would multiply by 2^32 per Link: beyond the ceiling at the second Link.
